            <ArticleTitle>Study of the cognitive component of nociception by the tail flick method.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>378-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The possibility of using the tail flick test as a model for studies of the cognitive component of nociception in rats was evaluated. The results were compared with the data of active avoidance test in a shuttle chamber. The results demonstrate the methodological potentialities of the tail flick test as a convenient model for training of animals in studies of the nociceptive reactions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
